  "notes": "Composed of {輸|ゆ} (transport) + {血|けつ} (blood). Used as both a noun and a suru verb.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {輸血|ゆけつ}を{受|う}ける: to receive a blood transfusion\n- {輸血|ゆけつ}する: to transfuse blood / to give a transfusion\n- {輸血|ゆけつ}が{必要|ひつよう}: a transfusion is necessary\n- {大量|たいりょう}の{輸血|ゆけつ}: a large transfusion\n- {輸血|ゆけつ}パック: blood transfusion bag\n\nRELATED MEDICAL 〜{血|けつ} TERMS:\n- {献血|けんけつ}: blood donation\n- {採血|さいけつ}: blood drawing, taking blood\n- {出血|しゅっけつ}: bleeding\n- {止血|しけつ}: stopping bleeding\n- {血液型|けつえきがた}: blood type",
